==Strategy==
The Gory Darks and Wall Doges have short range and decent money drops, so most of your firepower can come in the form of stackable, lower-cost mid-ranged attackers like [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]]. To take out Nyandam and Kurosawah, whittle them down with [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cats]]' [[Wave Attack|Waves]] or [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attacks]]; if you have a spare slot for [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], try to slip one through whenever the opportunity presents itself.

Unless you have [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], you can expect this fight to take a while, especially on higher difficulties.

